# config/db.js
Purpose
This file connects the application to MongoDB using Mongoose.
Responsibilities
- Reads the MongoDB connection URL from .env
- Establishes a connection to the database
- Stops the server if the connection fails
Usage
Imported and executed inside app.js

# controllers Folder
Controllers contain the business logic. They decide what happens when a request is received.
chatController.js
Handles AI chat requests.
What it does:
- Receives the user’s message
- Extracts data from the request body
- Calls aiService.js to get an AI response
- Optionally saves the conversation in MongoDB
- Sends the AI reply back to the frontend
This is where AI → Database → Response happens.
mealPlanController.js
Manages meal plan data.
What it handles:
- Generate a new meal plan using AI
- Save meal plans to MongoDB
- Fetch all meal plans
- Fetch a specific meal plan
- Delete a meal plan

# models Folder
Models define how data is stored in MongoDB.
ChatMessage.js
Schema for chat history. Each chat message includes:
- userId
- userMessage
- aiReply
- createdAt
This is optional but useful for chat history.
MealPlan.js
Schema for storing meal plans returned by AI. It contains:
- goal
- preferences
- plan (AI-generated JSON)
- userId
- createdAt
This structure matches exactly what the AI is instructed to return.

# routes Folder
Routes define which URL triggers which controller. Because Express is not used, routing is handled manually using if conditions.
chatRoutes.js
Defines chat-related endpoints. Examples:
- POST /api/chat/message
- GET /api/chat/history
Each request is forwarded to chatController.js.
mealPlanRoutes.js
Defines meal-plan-related endpoints. Examples:
- POST /api/meal-plan
- GET /api/meal-plan/latest
- GET /api/meal-plan/all
- GET /api/meal-plan/:id
- DELETE /api/meal-plan/:id
Each request is forwarded to mealPlanController.js.

# services Folder
This folder contains logic that is independent of routing and database.
aiService.js
Handles all communication with the AI.
Responsibilities:
- Sends structured prompts to the AI
- Forces the AI to return clean JSON
- Prevents messy or unstructured AI responses
- Returns the result to the controllers
This file is the brain of AI communication.

# app.js (Server Entry Point)
This is the main backend file.
What it does:
- Creates the HTTP server using http.createServer
- Handles CORS manually
- Routes incoming requests
- Connects to MongoDB
- Starts the backend server
This file wakes up the backend.

# .env File
Stores sensitive configuration values.
Examples:
- MongoDB connection URL
- Server port
- AI API key
This file is never committed to GitHub.

